(module crux-reports-drops-hist)
;; THE DROPPED SUPPRESSOR. `reports?` decides whether one citation is reported.
;; Six pieces of evidence suppress a report; this body consults five and drops
;; `hist`, the historical-line marker. The gate then reports every citation on a
;; past-tense line, which is the false-positive class the ALLOW table and the
;; history marker exist to prevent.
;;
;; This is the mutation tools/doc-path-lint/adjudicate.llmll names in its own
;; header. It is committed here because naming a refuting case in a comment is
;; not running one (TOOL-ORACLE-1).
;;
;; THE POST IS AN EQUALITY AND THAT IS WHY THIS IS CAUGHT. An implication in
;; either direction is satisfied by a body that reports everything or one that
;; reports nothing. Only the equality pins both directions.
;;
;; MEASURED at v0.16.2: REFUTED at constraint #0. The unmutated sibling reports
;; `body-faithful: reports?` and verifies SAFE.
(def reports? [root: bool rel: bool label: bool ph: bool allow: bool hist: bool] -> bool
  (post (= result (not (or (or (or root rel) (or label ph)) (or allow hist)))))
  (not (or (or (or root rel) (or label ph)) allow)))
